       "role": "system",
       "content": "",
       "sections": {
        "codemode": "<codemode>\nTools scripts can call (`await tools.<name>(args)`):\n\n### `echo`\necho\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { echo(args: { id?: number; text?: string; }): Promise<string>; };\n```\n\n### `hold`\nhold\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { hold(args: { id?: number; text?: string; }): Promise<string>; };\n```\n</codemode>"
       },
       "toolsAdded": [
        {
         "name": "codemode",
         "description": "Run JavaScript that calls other tools. The input is raw JavaScript (not JSON, no code fence), run as an async function body in a QuickJS sandbox: top-level `await` and `return` work. No Node, file system, network, or timers.\n- `await tools.<name>({ ...args })` resolves to a string, or an object if the tool's declaration says so, and rejects with an Error on failure. A tool whose declaration returns an object resolves on failure too when it returned that object; check its fields. Calls still running when the script ends are cancelled.\n- The script survives a restart: it resumes where it was, without running finished calls again.\n- Optional first line: `// @options: {\"max_output_tokens\": 10000, \"timeout_ms\": 60000}`\n\nGlobals:\n- `text(value)`, `image(dataUrlOrImageBlock)`, `console.log(...)`, and top-level `return` add output; `exit()` ends the script. With several text items, each starts with a `==> text N/M <==` line, and `console` lines follow the other output in one `<console_output>` block. `image()` also saves the image to a temp file and the result names its path.\n- `store(key, value)` and `load(key)` keep JSON values across codemode calls.\n- `ALL_TOOLS`, `await searchTools(query, { limit?, namespace? })`, `await describeTool(name)`, `await describeNamespace(name)`: find tools the `codemode` section does not list.\n\n`models` (all functions return promises):\n- `models.getModelsOfType(type, provider?)`, `models.getAvailableOfType(type, provider?)` (configured auth only), `models.getModelOfType(type, provider, id)`: the catalog; `type` is \"chat\", \"image\", or \"classifier\".\n- `models.classify(model, { state: { ... }, images?: [{ type: \"image\", data, mimeType }], questions: { <id>: { type: \"choice\", instructions, criteria: { <label>: <meaning> } } | { type: \"score\", instructions, criteria: [<lowest level>, ..., <highest level>] } | { type: \"bool\", instructions, criteria: { true: <meaning>, false: <meaning> } } } })` resolves to `{ answers: { <id>: ... }, stopReason, errorMessage?, usage? }`.\n- `models.generateImages(model, { input: [{ type: \"text\", text: <prompt> }, ...optional { type: \"image\", data, mimeType }] })` resolves to `{ output: [image blocks], stopReason, errorMessage?, usage? }`; show each image with `image(block)`.\nAt most 4 classify/generateImages calls run at once; more wait.\n\nThe `codemode` section of the system prompt lists the tools scripts can call, by namespace, as far as space allows.",
         "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
           "code"
          ],
          "properties": {
           "code": {
